  "narrative": "All new claims use direction -1, so positive signed estimates correspond to stronger dependency, i.e. a more negative CRISPR dependency score in the exposed group relative to the comparator. The low-benchmark outcomes outcome_006 and outcome_014 have a 10% absolute-mean threshold of about 0.0093, whereas outcome_015 and outcome_013 have thresholds near 0.025 and 0.027 respectively. The strongest remaining candidate is H118, feature_023=0 versus 1 on outcome_006, with signed estimate +0.0458, about 4.9 times the outcome_006 benchmark. H119, the parallel feature_023 test on outcome_014, is also positive and large at +0.0355, about 3.8 times the outcome_014 benchmark. The intervals still include null, with H118 closest to excluding null and H119 more imprecise, so neither can be accepted on discovery evidence. Because H118 is the most threshold-aligned and least null-inclusive of this feature_023 pair, I request independent validation of H118. If it validates, I will reconsider H119 and H3 as cross-outcome coherence; if it fails, the feature_023 low-benchmark signal should likely be closed.\n\nMost other new screens are not supported or are internally inconsistent. H103, outcome_014 feature_064, has a positive point estimate above the low benchmark, but its interval is wide and includes substantial null, so it remains unresolved and closed rather than accepted. H109, outcome_014 feature_030, is also positive but extremely imprecise, and prior feature_030 screens elsewhere were null or not threshold-aligned, so it is unresolved and closed. H112, outcome_006 feature_027, is null-to-opposite and does not support stronger dependency, so it is rejected. H113, outcome_014 feature_027, is a very large opposite association, with a tight interval entirely favoring weaker dependency rather than stronger dependency. This is a strong result against the proposed direction and could be worth a separate reversed investigation, but it cannot support the registered claim and may also reflect an extreme coding or distributional issue; I reject the current claim.\n\nThe feature_050 and feature_045 screens are not coherent. H114 is opposite on outcome_006, while H115 is positive but imprecise on outcome_014, so both are rejected as not supporting a stable low-benchmark effect. Similarly, H116 is positive on outcome_006 but H117 is opposite on outcome_014; the inconsistent cross-outcome pattern and interval uncertainty justify rejecting H116 as a meaningful association rather than spending validation on it. The feature_063 level_003 tests are opposite to the claimed direction on outcome_015 and outcome_013, and prior feature_063 level_002 tests were null, so H97 and H110 are rejected. Overall, these new low-benchmark screens leave feature_023 as the only plausible candidate, but the conclusion remains dataset-specific association and not causal or generalizable until validation.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 9 appraise update. Accepted set remains empty. Direction -1 positive signed means exposed group has stronger dependency, i.e. more negative outcome. Outcome_006/014 benchmark approx 0.0093; outcome_015 approx 0.025; outcome_013 approx 0.027. Candidate family: feature_023=0 versus 1. H118 outcome_006 signed +0.0458, CI -0.0023 to +0.0939; H119 outcome_014 signed +0.0355, CI -0.0123 to +0.0833; H3 outcome_003 signed +0.0080 below benchmark. Validation requested for H118 only. If H118 validation is positive and multiplicity-adjusted evidence remains clinically meaningful, accept H118 and reassess H119/H3 for coherence; if adjusted interval still includes null or is below benchmark, keep unresolved or reject depending on validation point. If H118 validation fails, close H118/H119 and deprioritize feature_023. Closed/rejected families: feature_027 due H113 huge opposite result and H112 null; feature_050 due H114 opposite and inconsistent with H115; feature_045 due H117 opposite despite H116 positive; feature_063 level_003 due opposite H97/H110 and null level_002; feature_030 low outcome due H109 imprecise and prior nulls; feature_064 low outcomes due imprecise positive intervals and no decisive threshold-level pattern. Active queue should now wait for H118 validation rather than continue broad screening unless validation produces a clear threshold-supported signal.",
